TensorFold patch 0006: the prompt cache on disk, and resume points at the last message starts.

Why: (1) a kept prompt state lived only in a GPU slot, so it was lost when the router switched models, when the
server restarted, or when more conversations than slots took turns; every such turn re-prefilled its whole history
(~15 s for 30k tokens). (2) Resume points were only after the system prompt and at the prompt end, so a client that
rewrites its newest message when it sends it back as history (e.g. an agent client that adds recalled memories to the newest user
message and leaves them out next turn) missed everything after the system prompt on every turn.

What:
- cuda/markers.py: TF_POINTS_LAST (default 0 = upstream) adds the last N message starts to the resume points; the
  recipe uses 3. The client's edit then costs one turn's tokens instead of the whole history.
- cuda/prompt_store.py (new, no family code): the store. index.sqlite + per model key content-addressed 1024-row
  blocks and point files; a writer thread (a bounded queue: a point that doesn't fit is skipped, never waited for);
  longest-prefix lookup through a 256-token hash chain; loads only when the measured read time beats recomputing;
  normal points (TF_PROMPT_CACHE_GIB, TTL hours since saved) and pinned ones (TF_PROMPT_CACHE_PIN_AFTER different
  continuations resumed from it; own budget, no TTL, never changed); pinned points of an older key are prefilled again
  through the server while it is idle. Tier = the file place (has/get/put/evict), the extension point for a NAS.
- families/qwen4_exp/cuda/disk_points.py (new): Flash Next's point <-> slot (attention rows, index keys, pools, MTP
  head, DeltaNet/conv/n-gram snapshot, MTP tail).
- families/qwen4_exp/cuda/multi.py: the store opens with the decoder (one GPU, TF_PROMPT_CACHE_DIR set); _slot_for
  first loads a better disk point into a free slot; _remember also queues the point for disk; warm() stays off disk.

Off unless TF_PROMPT_CACHE_DIR is set. Tests: tests/cuda/test_prompt_store.py (CPU).
Base: TensorFold 609ca419 + the recipe's vision-prefix-cache.patch + local 0001-0005.

